                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4Buyfiatonramp_e_55" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#CBD5E1;" parent="1" source="4Buyfiatonramp_c_48" target="4Buyfiatonramp_c_53" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4Buyfiatonramp_e_56" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#CBD5E1;" parent="1" source="4Buyfiatonramp_c_49" target="4Buyfiatonramp_c_53" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4Buyfiatonramp_c_57" value="(f) Purchased asset delivered on-chain&lt;br&gt;to the user&#39;s own wallet address&lt;br&gt;(same settlement pattern as path A)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=middle;fillColor=#4C1D6B;strokeColor=#C084FC;fontColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1298" y="1990" width="280" height="84" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4Buyfiatonramp_e_58" value="crypto" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#FB923C;strokeWidth=3;fontColor=#FDBA74;" parent="1" source="4Buyfiatonramp_c_53" target="4Buyfiatonramp_c_57" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4Buyfiatonramp_c_69" value="(i) PARTIES: user; Core Mobile app; Ava Labs backend (the Core proxy, which brokers all Meld traffic and signs Moonpay URLs); Meld as aggregator; the licensed payment service provider that actually sells the asset; the user&#39;s card issuer or bank; the blockchain network.&lt;br&gt;(ii) FLOW OF FUNDS: two legs that never meet inside Core. The FIAT leg runs from the user&#39;s card or bank account to the provider and stays entirely within the provider&#39;s regulated environment — no fiat enters an Ava Labs or Core-controlled account. The CRYPTO leg runs from the provider on-chain directly to the user&#39;s own wallet address. Purchasable assets include native coins (AVAX) and stablecoins (USDC on C-Chain).&lt;br&gt;(iii) CUSTODY: Core is non-custodial for both legs. It never holds customer fiat and never takes possession of the purchased crypto — settlement is provider-to-user. The app supplies only the destination address it derived at onboarding. No private key is used anywhere in this flow.&lt;br&gt;(iv) THIRD PARTIES: Meld (aggregation, quoting, session creation, webhook reconciliation) receives the wallet address, amount and currency pair. The selected provider additionally receives full KYC identity and payment credentials, collected in its own hosted widget — those credentials are never seen by the app. Legacy path: Moonpay, Coinbase Pay, Halliday. KYC and sanctions screening are performed by the provider, not by Core.&lt;br&gt;(v) FEES: the provider&#39;s fee and FX spread, shown in the quote before the user commits; the card or bank charge levied by the user&#39;s own issuer; and the network fee for the on-chain delivery, normally absorbed into the provider&#39;s quote. Whether Ava Labs receives any referral or revenue share from Meld or the providers is a commercial arrangement that is NOT observable in the client code and must be confirmed from the contracts." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#0B2545;strokeColor=#64748B;fontColor=#E2E8F0;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="2134" width="1500" height="310" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
