                <mxCell id="6StakeEarn_c_55" value="  (k) Key control boundary — funding" style="rounded=1;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#F87171;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontColor=#FCA5A5;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;dashPattern=8 8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="340" y="869" width="296" height="116" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="6StakeEarn_c_56" value="  (k) Key control boundary — claim" style="rounded=1;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#F87171;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontColor=#FCA5A5;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;dashPattern=8 8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="340" y="1699" width="296" height="116" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="6StakeEarn_c_57" value="  (f) Core-owned fee escrow — Fast Stake only" style="rounded=1;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FBBF24;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontColor=#FDE68A;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;dashPattern=8 8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="960" y="1139" width="296" height="128" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="6StakeEarn_c_68" value="(i) PARTIES: user; Core Mobile app; Ava Labs backend (Glacier validator data, PostHog fee-rate flag); the chosen validator node operator; a Core-owned P-Chain escrow address (Fast Stake only); the Avalanche C-Chain and P-Chain.&lt;br&gt;(ii) FLOW OF FUNDS: AVAX only, no fiat. Funding from the C-Chain requires two atomic cross-chain transactions (exportC then importP) before the delegation transaction itself. The stake is then locked for the chosen duration. Claiming reverses the direction with two further atomic transactions (exportP then importC). Every leg stays between addresses the user controls, except the Fast Stake convenience-fee output.&lt;br&gt;(iii) CUSTODY: non-custodial, with two points worth stating. First, the staked AVAX is locked by the Avalanche protocol itself — neither Core nor the validator can spend, seize, or redirect it, the validator never takes possession, but the funds are ILLIQUID for the full term and cannot be withdrawn early. Second, EVERY transaction in this flow is separately signed by the user: up to three signatures to fund and delegate, and TWO MORE to claim (exportP and importC are signed independently). Hardware wallets require a physical confirmation for each one. Because the flow spans several transactions, an interrupted run can leave AVAX in an atomic-transfer state; importAnyStuckFunds exists to recover it.&lt;br&gt;(iv) THIRD PARTIES: the validator node operator (earns and shares rewards, takes its own commission); Glacier supplies the validator metrics used for Fast Stake auto-selection. No customer identity data is shared with either.&lt;br&gt;(v) FEES: (1) C-Chain atomic transaction fee on exportC; (2) P-Chain fee on importP; (3) P-Chain delegation transaction fee; (4) the VALIDATOR&#39;s delegation fee (commission), deducted from rewards earned; (5) two further network fees when claiming (exportP and importC); and (6) on the FAST STAKE PATH ONLY, a CORE CONVENIENCE FEE paid to a Core-owned P-Chain escrow address as a UTXO output bundled with the delegation transaction. The rate is delivered as a PostHog multivariate flag variant in basis points and applied to the NET estimated reward after the validator&#39;s own fee; no variant configured means no fee. The reward shown to the user is net of this fee before they commit. THE ADVANCED DELEGATE PATH CHARGES NO CORE FEE — the client contains a separate, currently unenabled delegate-fee flag and escrow address, so the capability exists in code but is dormant; confirm its status before relying on this." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#0B2545;strokeColor=#64748B;fontColor=#E2E8F0;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="2210" width="1500" height="330" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
