                <mxCell id="9dApptransactionsigning_e_30" value="value leaves the&lt;br&gt;user&#39;s address" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#FB923C;strokeWidth=3;fontColor=#FDBA74;" parent="1" source="9dApptransactionsigning_c_14" target="9dApptransactionsigning_c_15" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="9dApptransactionsigning_e_31" value="tx hash" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#CBD5E1;" parent="1" source="9dApptransactionsigning_c_15" target="9dApptransactionsigning_c_16" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="9dApptransactionsigning_e_32" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#CBD5E1;" parent="1" source="9dApptransactionsigning_c_16" target="9dApptransactionsigning_c_17" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="9dApptransactionsigning_e_33" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#021640;strokeColor=#94A3B8;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#CBD5E1;" parent="1" source="9dApptransactionsigning_c_17" target="9dApptransactionsigning_c_18" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="9dApptransactionsigning_c_34" value="  (k) Key control boundary" style="rounded=1;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#F87171;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontColor=#FCA5A5;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;dashPattern=8 8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="340" y="1119" width="296" height="128" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="9dApptransactionsigning_c_45" value="(i) PARTIES: user; Core Mobile app (the WebView and the injected provider shim); Ava Labs backend (Blockaid proxy on the WalletConnect path); the third-party dApp and, where used, the WalletConnect relay; the blockchain network. Any smart contract the dApp calls is a further counterparty.&lt;br&gt;(ii) FLOW OF FUNDS: entirely determined by the dApp&#39;s transaction, not by Core. It may move native coins, stablecoins, other tokens or NFTs, grant a spending allowance, or move nothing at all (a plain message signature). No fiat. Core constructs none of it — the app decodes and presents what the dApp asked for.&lt;br&gt;(iii) CUSTODY: non-custodial, and the strongest per-transaction control in the wallet. Signing stays inside the key control boundary and EVERY dApp request reaches an explicit approval screen: the Quick Swaps auto-approve bypass requires an in-app request and is therefore structurally unreachable from a dApp. Approvals parked when the user navigates cross-origin are aborted rather than left live, and account addresses are disclosed only after the user authorises the specific site. The residual risk is not custodial but comprehension-based — a user may approve a transaction whose effect they misjudge, most consequentially an unlimited token allowance.&lt;br&gt;(iv) THIRD PARTIES: the dApp is an arbitrary, unvetted third party — this is the widest exposure surface in the wallet. Blockaid screens the dApp URL on the WalletConnect path, gated by a feature flag. NOTE: no equivalent Blockaid site scan was found on the in-app BROWSER path in the client code; if browser-side dApp screening is expected, that gap should be confirmed with engineering rather than assumed from this diagram.&lt;br&gt;(v) FEES: the network fee is the only cost Core is involved in, and it is paid to validators or miners. Core applies no service fee to a dApp transaction. Any additional cost — a swap fee, mint price, protocol fee, or spread — is set by the dApp&#39;s own contract and is outside Core&#39;s control and visibility." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#0B2545;strokeColor=#64748B;fontColor=#E2E8F0;fontFamily=Verdana;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="1610" width="1500" height="300" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>